{"base_rate":0.7833109017496636,"brier":0.17253337819650066,"bss":-0.01648714968730669,"bss_hi":0.09703331737458598,"bss_lo":-0.14942459646335882,"chart":{"base":[739.1,251.4],"fp":[733.3,324.5],"lead":"62,257.9 272,259.1 482,261.6 692,261.7","note":{"base":"skill -0.02 — higher than 11% of cities","fp":"low end +33pp, high end +2pp","lead":"day-1 error 1.0 °C — better than 62% of cities","rel":"promised 28% → rained 56%; promised 100% → rained 92%"},"rel":"237.9,224.3 446.6,141.3 564.3,130 645.4,83.3 689,68.7"},"country":"MP","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.11075370121130554,"ess":527.9484473892649,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Saipan</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Saipan rain forecast is cannot beat its own climatology, though 4 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (100%), believe about\n<b>92%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(17%), there is still roughly a <b>48%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 743 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nCAPITOL HILL 1, 0.4 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score -0.02, ranked 193 of\n216 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(177&ndash;203) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>17%</td><td class='num'><b>48%</b></td><td class='num'>73</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>39%</td><td class='num'><b>64%</b></td><td class='num'>70</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>56%</td><td class='num'><b>75%</b></td><td class='num'>77</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>67%</td><td class='num'><b>75%</b></td><td class='num'>68</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>77%</td><td class='num'><b>77%</b></td><td class='num'>83</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>84%</td><td class='num'><b>79%</b></td><td class='num'>61</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>90%</td><td class='num'><b>85%</b></td><td class='num'>86</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>96%</td><td class='num'><b>94%</b></td><td class='num'>63</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>100%</td><td class='num'><b>92%</b></td><td class='num'>162</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">4 of 9 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Saipan</b> <span class=\"muted\">Northern Mariana Islands</span></p>\n  <div class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag bad\">Cannot beat climatology</span><details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What does this label mean?\" title=\"What does this label mean?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>Compared with a simple guess: saying &ldquo;78% chance of rain&rdquo; every day, because it rains here on 78% of days.</p><p>The forecast did worse than that guess. The difference is within the margin of error.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details>\n    <span class=\"muted\">4 points off by more than chance</span></div>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score<details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What is the skill score?\" title=\"What is the skill score?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>How much better the forecast is than that simple guess. 0 means no better, 1 means perfect, below 0 means worse. Day-ahead rain forecasts usually score 0.3 to 0.5.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details></dt><dd>-0.02</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>177&ndash;203\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 216</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>743 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Saipan &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Saipan\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"118.56794520547945,287.26027397260276 196.768,194.8 254.67688311688312,140.79090909090976 296.06500000000005,98.29411764705884 329.4284337349398,70.62650602409639 354.9537704918033,47.8360655737705 378.12302325581396,30.697674418604606 396.26666666666665,18.0 410.3174074074074,18.0 410.3174074074074,24.740740740740705 396.26666666666665,52.666666666666686 378.12302325581396,77.25581395348837 354.9537704918033,113.47540983606558 329.4284337349398,136.40963855421688 296.06500000000005,178.58823529411765 254.67688311688312,221.27272727272728 196.768,283.2 118.56794520547945,347.09589041095893\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"96.87483176312247\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"96.87483176312247\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"118.56794520547945,207.47945205479454 196.768,147.99999999999997 254.67688311688312,107.81818181818181 296.06500000000005,109.0 329.4284337349398,101.32530120481925 354.9537704918033,95.57377049180326 378.12302325581396,73.02325581395348 396.26666666666665,41.111111111111086 410.3174074074074,47.20987654320987\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 17%&amp;#10;It rained 48% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 73 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"118.56794520547945\" cy=\"207.47945205479454\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 39%&amp;#10;It rained 64% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 70 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"196.768\" cy=\"147.99999999999997\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 56%&amp;#10;It rained 75% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 77 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"254.67688311688312\" cy=\"107.81818181818181\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 67%&amp;#10;It rained 75% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 68 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"296.06500000000005\" cy=\"109.0\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 77%&amp;#10;It rained 77% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 83 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"329.4284337349398\" cy=\"101.32530120481925\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 84%&amp;#10;It rained 79% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 61 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"354.9537704918033\" cy=\"95.57377049180326\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 90%&amp;#10;It rained 85% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 86 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"378.12302325581396\" cy=\"73.02325581395348\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 96%&amp;#10;It rained 94% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 63 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"396.26666666666665\" cy=\"41.111111111111086\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 100%&amp;#10;It rained 92% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 162 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"410.3174074074074\" cy=\"47.20987654320987\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(78%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Saipan the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>winter</b> (0.12) and least in\n<b>autumn</b> (-0.24).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>182</td><td class='num'>88%</td><td class='num'>-0.245</td><td class='num'>12.1%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>207</td><td class='num'>75%</td><td class='num'>-0.132</td><td class='num'>15.6%</td></tr><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>184</td><td class='num'>82%</td><td class='num'>-0.028</td><td class='num'>8.0%</td></tr><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>170</td><td class='num'>68%</td><td class='num'>0.118</td><td class='num'>9.7%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":15.21233,"lon":145.7545,"n":743,"n_cities":216,"name":"Saipan","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.31,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.17109589041095888,"n":73,"obs":0.4794520547945205,"sig":true},{"hi":0.49,"lo":0.31,"mean":0.392,"n":70,"obs":0.6428571428571429,"sig":true},{"hi":0.63,"lo":0.49,"mean":0.5555844155844156,"n":77,"obs":0.7532467532467533,"sig":true},{"hi":0.73,"lo":0.63,"mean":0.6725000000000001,"n":68,"obs":0.75,"sig":false},{"hi":0.81,"lo":0.73,"mean":0.7667469879518073,"n":83,"obs":0.7710843373493976,"sig":false},{"hi":0.88,"lo":0.81,"mean":0.8388524590163936,"n":61,"obs":0.7868852459016393,"sig":false},{"hi":0.94,"lo":0.88,"mean":0.9043023255813954,"n":86,"obs":0.8488372093023255,"sig":false},{"hi":0.98,"lo":0.94,"mean":0.9555555555555555,"n":63,"obs":0.9365079365079365,"sig":false},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.98,"mean":0.995246913580247,"n":162,"obs":0.9197530864197531,"sig":true}],"prcp_km":0.4,"provisional":false,"rank":193,"rank_hi":203.0,"rank_lo":177.0,"reliability":0.02172275536084015,"resolution":0.017689022906606365,"skill_pct":null,"slug":"saipan","station":"CAPITOL HILL 1","timezone":"Pacific/Saipan"}